# NetEpic rulebook source of truth

Baguettepic is a companion app for Palladium NetEpic 3. Game rules, army books, and LaTeX source live in a **local** checkout of the English translation — not on GitHub for day-to-day agent work.

## Canonical local folder

- Path: `C:\Files\NetEpicFR300-EnglishTranslation`
- Do **not** fetch rules from GitHub (`gh api`, raw GitHub URLs, or cloning) when this folder is available.
- Do **not** invent rules; read the matching `.tex` (or diagram) from this folder.

## Important folders

| Content | Path under the local folder |
|---|---|
| Core rulebook (LaTeX) | `Rulebook 303/` |
| Tyranids army book | `Tyranids 310/` |
| Exodites army book | `Exodites 300/` |
| Biel-Tan army book | `Biel-Tan 310/` |
| Necrons army book | `Necrons 310/` |
| Domain class diagram (schema inspiration) | `Rulebook 303/class-diagram.md` |

Key rulebook sections under `Rulebook 303/`:

- `00 - Intro/` — Important Concepts, Introduction, Preparing for Battle
- `01 - Game Turn/` — Strategy, Movement, Combat, End phases
- `02 - Something/` — Morale, Terrain, Titans and Praetorians
- `03 - Special Abilities/`
- `04 - Markers and Templates/`
- `main.tex` / `Preamble.tex` — document entry points

## Agent behavior

- When seeding or editing `Database/*.sql`, special abilities, or in-app rule text, read the matching `.tex` (or diagram) from `C:\Files\NetEpicFR300-EnglishTranslation`.
- Cite source paths relative to that folder (e.g. `Rulebook 303/01 - Game Turn/Combat Phase.tex`, `Tyranids 300/Unit Profiles.tex`).
- Keep long rule prose out of Cursor rules; point at the files instead.
- This app repo (`Baguettepic`) owns the MAUI client and MySQL seed/schema; the translation folder owns the printed-rules source.
